1
00:00:01,227 --> 00:00:19,217
Night in Seville. In the courtyard of the Commendatore's palace, a servant paces with a lantern. Leporello. He grumbles Notte e giorno faticar: toiling night and day for a master who never thanks him. Bad food, little sleep, he complains. I want to be the gentleman, he says, not the servant. Then he hears footsteps and hides.

2
00:00:20,537 --> 00:00:32,207
Out of the house runs a man wrapped in a long cloak, hiding his face. Clinging to him is Donna Anna, the Commendatore's daughter. Don't hope to escape, she cries, unless you kill me. Help! Who is this man? He will not say. She will not let go.

3
00:00:33,527 --> 00:00:49,807
Then her father comes, an old man with a sword and a light. Fight me, he says. The stranger refuses: he will not fight an old man. The Commendatore insists. Two blades in the dark, a few strokes, and the old man falls. What a crime, whispers Leporello. Before he dies, the stranger watches him, almost curious. Then he and Leporello slip away into the night.

4
00:00:51,327 --> 00:01:02,297
Donna Anna comes back with her betrothed, Don Ottavio, and finds her father in his blood. She faints. When she wakes, she pushes Ottavio away: Fuggi, crudele, fuggi, go, cruel man.

5
00:01:03,417 --> 00:01:11,267
He is the only one left to her, he answers, a husband and a father. Then swear, she says. Over the body they swear revenge on a man whose face nobody saw.

6
00:01:13,263 --> 00:01:23,563
Dawn on a street outside the city. Leporello, brave for once, tells his master the truth: your life is the life of a scoundrel. Don Giovanni only smiles, and hushes him. He smells something. A woman.

7
00:01:24,883 --> 00:01:40,103
A lady in a travelling dress comes out of the inn, singing Ah, chi mi dice mai: who will tell me where that monster is? The man who promised to marry her and broke his word. If I find him, she sings, I'll tear his heart out. A lady in distress, says Don Giovanni. Let us go and console her.

8
00:01:41,423 --> 00:01:54,503
He bows, she turns, and they are face to face. It is Donna Elvira of Burgos. He came to her house, called her his wife, and left after three days. She has followed him across Spain. He listens, unmoved. Then he tells Leporello: you tell her everything. And he is gone.

9
00:01:55,823 --> 00:02:04,173
Leporello pulls out a long book. Madamina, il catalogo è questo: little lady, here is the list of the women my master has loved.

10
00:02:04,893 --> 00:02:12,943
In Italy, six hundred and forty. In Germany, two hundred and thirty-one. A hundred in France. Ninety-one in Turkey. But in Spain, already one thousand and three.

11
00:02:13,763 --> 00:02:26,263
He praises a blonde for her kindness, a dark-haired one for her faithfulness. Countesses, maids, a baroness, a farm girl: rich or poor, old or young, as long as she wears a skirt, you know what he does. Elvira stands alone in the street, and swears revenge.

12
00:02:28,257 --> 00:02:41,147
A country road, a village wedding. Giovinette che fate all'amore: young girls in love, don't let the time slip by. Zerlina, in a wreath of flowers, and her groom Masetto dance with their friends. Don Giovanni sees the bride.

13
00:02:42,367 --> 00:03:01,217
What a lovely face. He invites them all to his palace: Leporello, give them chocolate, coffee, wine and ham. Everyone except the bride, who stays with him. Masetto refuses. Don Giovanni touches his sword. Masetto understands at once: Ho capito, signor sì, I've understood, yes, my lord. And he goes, warning Zerlina that she will be sorry.

14
00:03:02,437 --> 00:03:22,837
Alone with her, Don Giovanni says a pretty face like hers is not made for a peasant. He will marry her himself, today, in his little house nearby. Là ci darem la mano: there we will give each other our hands. Zerlina wavers: Vorrei e non vorrei, I would and I would not. My heart trembles a little. Then, together: Andiam, let us go.

15
00:03:24,057 --> 00:03:39,657
Two steps from the gate, a voice: Stop, villain! It is Donna Elvira. She tells the girl everything: Ah, fuggi il traditor, run from the traitor, don't believe his words. Then she takes Zerlina by the hand and leads her away, leaving Don Giovanni alone on the road, for once without a woman.

16
00:03:41,650 --> 00:03:52,850
Donna Anna, in black mourning, walks with Don Ottavio. They meet a friend, a nobleman of the town: Don Giovanni. They ask him for help in finding her father's killer. Of course, he says. My sword, my house, my heart are yours.

17
00:03:54,470 --> 00:04:12,070
Then Donna Elvira appears. Non ti fidar, o misera: don't trust him, poor lady, that wicked heart has betrayed me. Don Giovanni lowers his voice to the others: the poor girl is mad. Elvira swears she is not. Anna and Ottavio look from one to the other. Don Giovanni leads Elvira away before she makes a scene.

18
00:04:13,690 --> 00:04:25,300
Before he goes, he turns back to Donna Anna. If you need me, he says, I am yours. Goodbye. She goes white. Don Ottavio, I am dying, she whispers. That voice. That is the voice of the man in the cloak. That is the man who killed my father.

19
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:51,550
And she tells Ottavio the whole night. It was late. She was alone in her room. A man in a cloak came in, and in the dark she thought he was Ottavio. Then he seized her. She fought, she screamed, she tore herself free and followed him out, and her father came. Or sai chi l'onore: now you know who tried to take my honour, who killed my father. I ask you for revenge; your own heart asks it. Ottavio cannot believe that a nobleman could do such a thing. He will watch Don Giovanni, and find the truth.

20
00:04:53,557 --> 00:05:04,517
Leporello reports: he took all the peasants to the palace, filled them with wine, and when Donna Elvira came to spoil everything, he led her out to the street and locked the door. Perfect, says his master. Now a great party.

21
00:05:05,437 --> 00:05:18,557
Fin ch'han dal vino: while the wine warms their heads, let them dance, the minuet, the follia, the German dance. If you meet a pretty girl in the square, bring her along too. And by tomorrow morning, my list must be longer by ten.

22
00:05:19,877 --> 00:05:37,977
In the garden, Masetto sulks. Zerlina knows how to win him back. Nothing happened, she swears: he did not even touch the tips of my fingers. Batti, batti, o bel Masetto: beat me, dear Masetto, I'll stand here like a little lamb. Pull my hair, put out my eyes. Then let us make peace, and spend our days and nights in joy. Masetto melts.

23
00:05:38,797 --> 00:05:46,197
Then he hears that voice, and hides. Don Giovanni finds Zerlina, and then finds Masetto too. He takes them both into the ballroom on his arms.

24
00:05:47,517 --> 00:05:58,487
Nightfall. Three guests arrive in masks and black cloaks: Donna Anna, Don Ottavio, Donna Elvira. Leporello, at the window, sees three masked ladies and gentlemen. My master would like you to come to the dance, he calls.

25
00:05:59,407 --> 00:06:08,797
They accept. At the door they stop, and pray together. Protegga il giusto cielo: may just heaven protect us. They have come to unmask a murderer, in his own house.

26
00:06:10,790 --> 00:06:24,840
The ballroom is full of candles and peasants. Don Giovanni greets the three masked guests himself. Come in, come in, lovely masks! The house is open to everyone, he cries. Viva la libertà! Long live freedom! And the masks sing it back to him, through their teeth.

27
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:45,100
Then the music. Three bands play at the same time, three dances in three different rhythms: an elegant minuet for the nobles, a country dance, and a fast German dance. Donna Anna can barely stand it. Pretend, Don Ottavio whispers. In the crowd, Don Giovanni dances with Zerlina, while Leporello grabs Masetto and makes him dance. Step by step, Don Giovanni moves Zerlina towards a door. And they are gone.

28
00:06:46,420 --> 00:06:59,270
A scream from the next room. Help! The guests break down the door. Out comes Don Giovanni, sword drawn, dragging Leporello by the collar. Here is the villain who insulted you, he shouts. I'll kill him. Nobody believes it. The wretch, they say, thinks a trick will hide his crime.

29
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:11,670
The three guests take off their masks. Donna Elvira. Donna Anna. Don Ottavio, with a pistol in his hand. Traditore! Traitor! We know everything now. Thunder over his head, they sing, the whole world will know.

30
00:07:12,590 --> 00:07:24,320
Elvira, Anna, Ottavio, Zerlina and Masetto close in around him. Don Giovanni looks at them all, and is not afraid. Even if the world fell, he says, nothing would make me tremble. Sword in hand, he walks through them, and out into the night.

31
00:07:26,323 --> 00:07:52,123
Leporello has had enough. I'm leaving, he says, you nearly got me killed. Come now, you clown, says Don Giovanni, and hands him four gold coins. Leporello stays. Just one thing, he says: give up women. Give up women? his master laughs. Women are more necessary to me than the bread I eat, more than the air I breathe. Who is faithful to one, he explains, is cruel to all the others. And tonight he wants Elvira's maid. Servants trust servants, so the two men change clothes: Leporello gets the cloak and the hat with the white plumes.

32
00:07:53,443 --> 00:08:16,983
Donna Elvira stands at her window in the evening. Ah, taci, ingiusto core: be quiet, unjust heart, don't beat for him. Hidden behind Leporello, Don Giovanni sings up to her: forgive me, Elvira, come down. Leporello waves his arms to match the words. I repent, he sings, I'll die if you don't believe me. Leporello can hardly keep from laughing. That lying mouth is at it again, he mutters; heaven protect her. And Elvira, against all reason, against everything she knows, believes him and comes down.

33
00:08:18,303 --> 00:08:38,963
Leporello, in his master's cloak, leads her away into the dark, terrified she will look at his face. Don Giovanni stays under the window with a mandolin. Deh, vieni alla finestra: come to the window, my treasure, come and take away my tears. Your mouth is sweeter than honey, he sings. A light moves in the maid's room. Someone is coming. He sings softer, and waits in the dark below the balcony.

34
00:08:40,943 --> 00:08:54,833
Instead of the maid comes Masetto, with village men armed with muskets and clubs. They are hunting Don Giovanni. In Leporello's clothes he joins the hunt. Half of you go that way, he orders, half this way. Masetto, you stay with me. He takes Masetto's musket and pistol, and beats him with them.

35
00:08:56,333 --> 00:08:57,523
Then he is gone.

36
00:08:58,843 --> 00:09:13,783
Zerlina hears Masetto groaning and comes with a lantern. Oh, my head, he moans, my shoulders. Vedrai, carino: you'll see, my darling, if you are good, I know a cure. It costs nothing, no chemist has it. She takes his hand and puts it on her heart. Feel it beating. That is the cure.

37
00:09:15,103 --> 00:09:32,043
In a dark courtyard, the real Leporello is still trying to lose Donna Elvira. Alone in this dark place, she sings, my heart is pounding. He finds a door, but Donna Anna and Ottavio come in by it. He turns: Zerlina and Masetto. In the plumed hat, they all take him for Don Giovanni. Kill him, they cry. No, begs Elvira: he is my husband, have pity.

38
00:09:33,363 --> 00:09:55,103
Leporello falls to his knees and pulls off the hat. Ah, pietà, signori miei! Perdono, perdono! Forgive me, it's only me! A servant, not a master. While they stare, he slips away. Now Ottavio knows, and decides: he will go to the law. Il mio tesoro: meanwhile, comfort my treasure, dry her tears. I am going to avenge her, and I will come back with news of his death.

39
00:09:57,083 --> 00:10:14,273
A walled burial ground, a night of moonlight brighter than the day. Don Giovanni has jumped over the wall to escape. Leporello finds him there, still in each other's clothes. His master is laughing: tonight, in the street, a girl took him for Leporello and called him darling. What if it was my wife? cries Leporello. Better still, laughs Don Giovanni, louder. Ah ah ah, this is a good one.

40
00:10:15,793 --> 00:10:39,313
A voice from the darkness: Di rider finirai pria dell'aurora. You will stop laughing before the dawn. Insolent wretch, the voice goes on, leave the dead in peace. Who spoke? Among the tombs stands a white marble statue, armoured, a stone sword in its hand: the Commendatore. The lantern shakes in Leporello's hand. Trembling, he holds it up and reads the words carved on its base: here I await revenge on the wicked man who brought me to my death. Leporello wants only to run.

41
00:10:40,833 --> 00:11:10,303
Don Giovanni laughs at the old fool. Tell him, he orders Leporello, that I invite him to supper tonight. Leporello refuses, until his master's sword is at his back. Shaking, he bows to the stone. O statua gentilissima: oh most noble statue. He cannot finish the sentence. The statue nods its head. Did you see? Don Giovanni does not believe it. He speaks to it himself. Will you come to supper? And the stone answers: Sì. Even Don Giovanni stops for a moment. Strange indeed, he says. Then he shrugs. Let us go home and prepare the supper.

42
00:11:12,290 --> 00:11:24,670
Candles, a laid table, a little band playing the hits of the day: Cosa rara, and then a tune Leporello knows only too well, Non più andrai, from The Marriage of Figaro. Leporello steals pheasant.

43
00:11:25,690 --> 00:11:37,830
Donna Elvira bursts in and kneels. She asks only that he change his life. He laughs, and drinks: Vivan le femmine, viva il buon vino! Long live women, long live good wine. She goes to the door, and screams.

44
00:11:38,850 --> 00:11:55,270
Leporello looks out and comes back white. The stone man, he says. Ta ta ta ta: those are his steps. A knock. Leporello hides under the table. The Commendatore fills the doorway. Don Giovanni, a cenar teco: you invited me to supper, and I have come. Will you come to supper with me? I will come.

45
00:11:56,290 --> 00:12:02,630
Give me your hand on it. He gives it. What cold is this? Pentiti! Repent! No! Repent! No! The statue lets go.

46
00:12:03,650 --> 00:12:12,720
Fire comes from every side, the floor opens, a chorus from below: all this is little for your crimes. Who is tearing my soul? he cries. Don Giovanni goes down into the abyss.

47
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:26,810
The others come too late. Donna Anna asks Ottavio for one more year. Elvira goes to a convent. Zerlina and Masetto go home to dinner. Leporello, to the inn, to find a better master. And all of them sing: this is the end of those who do evil.
